<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="skill">toxicity</ansi>

Every potion you drink adds toxicity to your body. Your tolerance
is based on your Vitality — hardier characters can handle more.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ How It Works ━━━</ansi>

  Drinking a potion adds its toxicity cost to your total.
  Toxicity decays naturally over time, a little each round.
  If your total would exceed your maximum, your body rejects
  the potion and it is not consumed.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Threshold Effects ━━━</ansi>

  At low toxicity, there are no ill effects. As it builds:
  - Moderate toxicity dulls your senses and slows recovery.
  - High toxicity further impairs your reflexes.
  - Severe toxicity significantly hampers regeneration and
    awareness.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Spoiled Potions ━━━</ansi>

  Drinking a spoiled potion inflicts triple the normal toxicity
  and causes nausea. Skilled alchemists can detect spoiled brews
  by examining them — look for the telltale signs.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Purging ━━━</ansi>

  The purging draught (alchemy skill 35) clears all active potion
  effects and toxicity, but leaves you weakened afterward.

